WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:07.200
Game of Thrones Season 8 Episode 3 is The
Long Night – the army of the dead attacks

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.330
Winterfell.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:13.540
The living are Daenerys and Jon with the dragons,
the Dothraki and Unsullied, armies of the

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.320
north Vale and wildlings, and almost every
other living character.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.890
Bran is with Theon in the godswood, cause
the plan is to lure the Night King and kill

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.600
him to end the war.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.000
So the whole gang’s here, fighting to save
the world.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.829
And they use some questionable battle tactics
.

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:36.800
Their trebuchets are in front of their defences,
so they only get to fire once before they’re

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.700
overwhelmed and useless.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.500
The infantry are in front of the trenches,
so the trenches don’t protect them, in fact

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.690
they get in the way of the retreat.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.890
You’d think everyone shoulda just stayed
in Winterfell, defending the castle, cause

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.950
that’s what castles are for.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:57.400
There are lots of weird tactics this episode,
made for the sake of heightening the drama.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.280
Melisandre arrives.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.950
She left for Volantis last season , and some
fans hoped she’d return with an army, or

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.760
other red priests.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.829
Melisandre doesn’t bring allies, but she
does bring fire magic, setting alight the

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:12.600
Dothraki weapons.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.380
It sure is lucky she came, because those Dothraki
arakhs aren’t Valyrian steel or dragonglass,

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.600
so they would’ve been pretty useless against
the dead if Mel hadn’t shown up.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.789
Melisandre’s confronted by Davos – he
once promised to execute Mel because she burned

00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:29.580
his friend Shireen.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.399
She says there’s no need to kill her because
she’ll die tonight.

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:38.880
There’s this great shot of Melisandre’s
shadow in the light – Melisandre believes

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.759
in just good and evil, black and white with
nothing in-between . But ironically, Melisandre

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:49.420
is one of the most morally grey characters
in the series – she does great things and

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.100
terrible things, and everything in between.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.899
The Dothraki charge, lights in the darkness
like stars – that blink out one by one as

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:00.399
the Dothraki die.

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:06.109
It’s a terrifying apocalyptic image that
also evokes Dothraki religion.

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:11.569
The Dothraki believe that when they die, their
spirit becomes a star , riding a fiery horse

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:17.820
across the night sky . The more fiercely a
man burns in life, the brighter his star shines

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:25.320
. So it’s all the more horrifying that these
fiery Dothraki are extinguished in pitch darkness.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.950
The showrunners say this is “the end of
the Dothraki” – which is a pretty bleak

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.840
end to their journey.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.629
Daenerys spent whole seasons winning the trust
of the Dothraki.

00:02:35.629 --> 00:02:39.939
She learned to be a Khaleesi, and led her
khalasar through the Red Waste.

00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:44.830
In Season 6, she returned to the Dothraki
and gathered a massive army, declaring them

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:50.600
all her personal blood riders , to cross the
seas and conquer as no other Dothraki had

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:57.180
– to be hers “Now and always” . But
ten minutes in to this battle, they’re all

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.180
dead.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.219
We never got to see the Dothraki perspective
on foreign Westeros, or how the Dothraki habit

00:03:03.219 --> 00:03:06.489
of burning and raiding would fit in Dany’s
regime.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:11.770
There weren’t even any named Dothraki this
season – unless you count Qhono, and no

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.349
one counts Qhono.

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:20.180
So this is a sad sudden end to the people
who shaped so much of Daenerys’ story.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.950
The plan is to keep the dragons out of combat
until the Night King comes , but when Dany

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:30.100
sees the Dothraki die, she abandons the plan,
and she and Jon burn some zombies, as they

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.880
should’ve from the start.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:36.290
Jon tries to attack the white walkers who
lead the dead, but the walkers conjure a storm

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.090
that blows him back – similar to the storm
at Hardhome.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.260
The dead crash into the living like an unstoppable
force of nature.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:50.610
Jaime Brienne Pod Tormund Beric Hound Gendry
Sam and Edd are all on the front lines, and

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:55.480
somehow they all survive this – except for
Edd, which is just his luck.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.859
RIP to the 999th Lord Commander of the Night’s
Watch.

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:05.450
The fighters realise that that castle thing
was a good idea after all, so they retreat

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.359
into Winterfell, while the Unsullied hold
back the dead.

00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:13.150
The Unsullied are uniquely qualified for this
sort of thing.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.449
In Game of Thrones history, a group of three
thousand Unsullied famously held off an army

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:19.600
of Dothraki at Qohor.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:25.169
Twenty thousand Dothraki broke on the Unsullied
“like waves on a rocky shore” . So the

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:30.150
Unsullied are good this, but they can only
last so long against the dead.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:35.260
So Grey Worm closes the trench behind his
men, sacrificing them.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:41.110
So very early in this battle, most of Daenerys’
army is destroyed – her Dothraki and Unsullied

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.639
are mostly gone.

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:48.200
So afterwards, she’ll need the support of
the north more than ever.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:52.750
The living try to the light the trench with
fiery torches – it’s a like a reverse

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.360
of Helm’s Deep from Lord of the Rings.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.780
The torches fail, so Melisandre steps up.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:03.120
Mel had a crisis of faith after Stannis died
in Season 5.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.490
She regained some confidence when she resurrected
Jon.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.710
And now, she calls on her god to give her
fire, and the trenches light.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:17.500
So Melisandre is filled with faith – she
believes her god has a plan.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.050
In the godswood, Bran uses his warging powers
to control some ravens, and he flies them

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.620
up to the Night King, on his zombie dragon.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:29.039
It’s unclear if Bran is trying to get the
Night King’s attention, or if he’s just

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:34.610
having a look-see, or what, but Bran spends
the rest of the battle in warg-mode, doing

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.569
nothing that we can see.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.160
Which seems like a waste of his powers.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:46.009
Bran spent six seasons learning magic to fight
the walkers – and now he’s not using any?

00:05:46.009 --> 00:05:52.039
He doesn’t warg a dragon, or have some important
vision, or tell anyone anything useful?

00:05:52.039 --> 00:05:57.069
It seems like Bran knows the future, he knows
how this battle will end, and he’s just

00:05:57.069 --> 00:05:59.960
sitting and watching while destiny runs it
course.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:07.680
So it’s pretty underwhelming that the culmination
of Bran’s training is him being bait – a

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.430
MacGuffin on wheels.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:14.190
Did Jojen and Hodor and Bran’s personality
die for this?

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.910
The dead are held back by the fiery trench,
but the Night King orders them to form a bridge

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.240
of corpses.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.470
Part of why the wights are scary is that they
have human bodies, but no humanity – they’re

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:29.800
just mindless machines with no self-preservation,
and no mercy.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.349
The dead assault the walls, and the heroes
hack and slash.

00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:37.910
A bunch of times, we see characters facing
certain death, covered in wights, but then

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:42.720
someone saves them with one sword-stoke, or
the camera just cuts, and it’s scary the

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:48.099
first few times, but it’s soon clear that
none of the main characters are in danger.

00:06:48.099 --> 00:06:54.050
Lyanna Mormont, the young Lady of Bear Isle,
dies killing a wight giant.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.139
Lyanna had always talked big talk.

00:06:56.139 --> 00:07:01.660
Now, she follows through with action, giving
her life to defend the north.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:06.000
There are hints in the books that Tormund
might be Lyanna’s father – go watch that

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.000
video.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.440
So it’s cool that last episode, Tormund
claimed to have killed a giant . Now, his

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.550
possible daughter Lyanna has also killed a
giant – must run in the family.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.830
The Hound freaks out – he’s afraid of
fire, since his brother the Mountain burned

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:21.879
his face.

00:07:21.879 --> 00:07:26.150
In Season 2, the Hound ran from the Battle
of Blackwater because of this fear.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:31.599
But when the Hound sees Arya in trouble, he
overcomes his fear, and rushes to help her.

00:07:31.599 --> 00:07:36.370
So again, Arya inspires the Hound be a braver
better man.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:41.409
Arya does some sick ninja moves, using all
her training with the Faceless Men – they

00:07:41.409 --> 00:07:44.449
taught her to fight with staffs, and in the
dark.

00:07:44.449 --> 00:07:49.539
But she takes a blow to the head, and retreats
to the Winterfell library for a stealth section,

00:07:49.539 --> 00:07:52.020
like the kitchen scene in Jurrasic Park.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:56.360
She silently kills a wight, and gently lowers
it to the ground.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.780
This is an intimate dance with death.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:03.360
Arya’s arc is all about the deaths of her
friends, the deaths of her enemies – now

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.530
she gets dangerously close to her own death
. When she’s overwhelmed, the Hound and

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.949
Beric save her.

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:14.370
Beric gives up his last life, sacrificing
himself in a Jesus T-pose.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:19.940
Beric believed the Lord of Light had a special
plan for him, and that’s why he was resurrected

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.360
six times.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.360
Turns out Beric’s destiny was to save Arya.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:28.690
You’d think that god could’ve cut out
the middle-man and just resurrected Arya if

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.860
needed – but since when were gods efficient?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.229
Arya sees Melisandre – they met before,
in Season 3.

00:08:36.229 --> 00:08:41.719
Melisandre had told Arya she would shut many
eyes forever – including “blue eyes”

00:08:41.719 --> 00:08:47.000
. She also reminds Arya of something Syrio
said – “What do we say to the God of Death?”,

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:53.240
“Not today” . So Mel is hinting that Arya’s
destiny is to kill the Night King, the blue-eyed

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.540
embodiment of death.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:59.200
Of course, these scenes were shot before the
showrunners decided to have Arya kill the

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:04.339
Night King, so they’re sorta retconned into
seeming relevant – Melisandre changes the

00:09:04.339 --> 00:09:09.670
wording of the eyes quote to emphasise the
blue eyes . The series spent seven seasons

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.180
setting up Jon and Dany as the forces to beat
the white walkers.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:17.830
But now at the last minute they shoehorn Arya
in as though she was foreshadowed from the

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.240
start.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.380
In the skies, the dragons dance.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:26.460
There hasn’t been a dragon fight in Westeros
for over a hundred years, and there’s never

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.710
been a fight with a zombie dragon.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:33.690
Daenerys’ dragon wounds the zombie dragon
Viserion, ripping off half his face.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:38.970
But Jon’s dragon Rhaegal is also hurt, and
crashes with Jon to the ground.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:45.120
Daenerys’ dragon burns the Night King, but
he’s unhurt, and smirks like an anime villain.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:50.029
Jon chases the Night King on foot, so the
Night King raises all the dead as zombies.

00:09:50.029 --> 00:09:54.440
Edd, Lyanna and Qhono all rise to fight their
former allies, which would be much scarier

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.440
if these guys were important characters.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:00.220
Jon is completely surrounded by zombies, but
when the camera cuts back, he’s fine.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:05.610
Jon has survived so many unsurvivable situations
lately that it’s getting hard to care when

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.220
he’s in danger.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:12.160
Daenerys lands her dragon, and it’s swarmed
by zombies, like ants over a lizard.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.990
Daenerys falls off Drogon – she should really
strap herself on to a saddle, like the old

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.280
Targaryens did.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.950
Jorah’s khaleesi-sense tingles, and he rushes
to help her.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:26.430
Jorah ultimately dies protecting Daenerys,
which is about the best death he could’ve

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.430
hoped for.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:33.230
He’s always been defined by his loyalty
to his khaleesi, so he dies as he lived.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:38.100
Meanwhile, Tyrion Sansa Missandei Varys and
Gilly hide in the crypts.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.810
Tyrion wants to help the battle somehow, but
Sansa says they can’t do anything, so they

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:43.810
don’t.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.610
Tyrion jokes that he and Sansa should’ve
stayed married, but Sansa says it wouldn’t

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:52.500
work because of Tyrion’s “divided loyalties”
– he’s more loyal to Daenerys than to

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.700
the Starks.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:58.639
The show seems to be setting up conflict between
Daenerys’ squad and Jon’s, and Tyrion

00:10:58.639 --> 00:11:00.830
is at its centre.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:05.610
When the Night King raises the dead, the dead
Starks in the crypts also rise – who would’ve

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.980
thought that a room full of corpses would
be dangerous with an icy necromancer on the

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:10.980
loose.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:15.730
Sansa and Tyrion share a moment of tenderness,
holding dragonglass daggers.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:19.230
Some viewers saw this like they were about
to kill themselves, but a behind-the-scenes

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:24.279
feature suggests they’re actually about
fight the zombies in some cut footage.

00:11:24.279 --> 00:11:28.639
The living are overwhelmed by the dead, and
Jon tries to get to Bran.

00:11:28.639 --> 00:11:33.529
He sees Sam almost killed by wights, but doesn’t
help him, which in bird culture is considered

00:11:33.529 --> 00:11:34.860
a dick more.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.220
Jon ends up pinned by the wounded zombie dragon.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:42.399
Fire streams from its neck, where it was bit
by Drogon.

00:11:42.399 --> 00:11:47.470
The walkers reach the godswood, and Theon
is the last ironborn standing.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:52.700
Bran tells Theon that he’s a good man , and
that Winterfell is his home . All Theon ever

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:56.589
wanted was a home, and a family that accepted
him.

00:11:56.589 --> 00:12:01.410
That tension is what led him to betray the
Starks, and take Winterfell from Bran.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.480
But now Bran forgives him.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:08.390
Theon finally gets his redemption, and is
killed by the Night King.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:14.730
In Book 5, Theon stands in this godswood and
prays for a sword – “Let me die as Theon,

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:19.170
not as Reek” . Now, he gets his wish.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:24.470
The Night King approaches Bran in ultra slow
motion – he’s waited eight thousand years

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.990
for this, so like any super villain, he takes
his sweet time.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:34.690
He and Bran and represent powerful magic forces
– Bran the three-eyed raven holds the world’s

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:39.589
memory and history, whatever that means, and
the Night King is an ancient weapon who turned

00:12:39.589 --> 00:12:42.010
on his creators, the children of the forest.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:47.930
Just as he’s about to kill Bran, Arya leaps
out of nowhere and attacks.

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:52.949
The Night King catches Arya, but she drops
her dagger into her off hand, and stabs the

00:12:52.949 --> 00:12:58.080
Night King – in the same place where the
dragonglass that created him was stabbed.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:04.270
Arya’s Valyrian knife was originally used
in an attempt on Bran’s life – now Arya

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:07.029
uses the knife to save Bran’s life.

00:13:07.029 --> 00:13:11.839
And the knife has a much older history – Sam
once found a book connecting the knife to

00:13:11.839 --> 00:13:15.769
the ancient Targaryens who took Westeros three
hundred years ago.

00:13:15.769 --> 00:13:20.579
The showrunners hinted that the hilt of this
blade is made from the same chunk of dragonglass

00:13:20.579 --> 00:13:26.149
that created the Night King – and so he
was unmade by the same dragonglass that created

00:13:26.149 --> 00:13:29.990
him .
The Night King is destroyed, and all his walkers

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:33.389
and wights also fall – like in the Phantom
Menace.

00:13:33.389 --> 00:13:38.769
Arya ends the Great War, and Melisandre walks
out into the dawn.

00:13:38.769 --> 00:13:41.880
She dedicated her life to winning this war.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:46.100
She is hundreds of years old, essentially
a slave to her god.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:51.410
Now, with her purpose finally fulfilled, she
lets herself rest.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:56.700
She reverts to her true ancient form, and
dies in the snow.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:14:02.339
So this episode brings a neat end the arcs
of Melisandre, Theon and Jorah.

00:14:02.339 --> 00:14:06.920
But what does it mean for the main characters,
and the white walkers, and Game of Thrones

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.550
itself?

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:12.860
In recent seasons, there’s a lot of foreshadowing
leading up to Arya killing the Night King

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.230
in the godswood.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:19.800
Bran gave Arya her Valyrian knife in the godswood
last season, and you can tell he had a special

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.339
purpose in mind.

00:14:21.339 --> 00:14:26.279
Then Arya sneaks up on Jon in the godswood
, just as she sneaks up on the Night King.

00:14:26.279 --> 00:14:30.899
And Arya uses the same hand-switching trick
with the knife on Brienne that she uses on

00:14:30.899 --> 00:14:32.079
the Night King.

00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:36.089
Arya trained for seasons to be a stealthy
deadly assassin.

00:14:36.089 --> 00:14:40.820
Her story is about death, and the Night King
is the embodiment of death.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:46.220
Maybe now that she’s killed him, Arya can
let go of her vengeance quest, and reconnect

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.100
with her humanity.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:53.459
So from the perspective of Arya’s story,
her killing the Night King makes sense.

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:56.259
But what does it mean for Jon and Dany?

00:14:56.259 --> 00:15:01.440
It’s clear from the start that Jon and Daenerys
are central to the magic and prophecy in this

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.709
story – the song of ice and fire.

00:15:04.709 --> 00:15:10.800
Daenerys was miraculously reborn unburnt with
dragons beneath a bleeding star.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:15.890
Jon Snow was resurrected like Christ, he’s
been fighting the dead since Season 1, and

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.660
he’s faced off the Night King repeatedly.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:23.670
Jon and Dany both come from the ancient magic
Targaryen bloodline, and there’s a prophecy

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:28.980
hinting that they will save the world from
the white walkers, with some magic sacrifice.

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:32.660
The show doesn’t mention the prophecy stuff
as much as the books do, but it’s still

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:36.970
heavily hinted that defeating the walkers
is Jon and Dany’s destiny.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:42.509
So it’s pretty crazy that Jon and Dany not
only don’t kill the Night King, but they’re

00:15:42.509 --> 00:15:47.600
barely involved in the end – like, while
Arya saves the world, Dany’s crying over

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:51.220
Ser Friendzone, and Jon is.. yelling at a
dragon.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.540
It’s not clear if Jon and Dany really helped
beat the walkers at all.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:16:00.130
Like, yeah they gathered the armies and helped
fight the dead, but that was always a losing

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:05.390
battle , just a ploy to lure the Night King
. If Jon and Dany weren’t there at all,

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:10.430
the Night King still would’ve come for Bran,
and Arya still could’ve killed him, right?

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:16.029
Jon and Dany represent the song of ice and
fire, yet they played only minor roles in

00:16:16.029 --> 00:16:17.579
its climax.

00:16:17.579 --> 00:16:22.240
The showrunners said they had Arya kill the
Night King because it was unexpected . And

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:26.510
Game of Thrones has always had surprising
twists – like when the ‘main character’

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:29.120
Ned Stark died in Season 1.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.009
And the deaths of Catelyn and Robb at the
Red Wedding.

00:16:32.009 --> 00:16:33.560
But those twists had meaning.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:38.569
They showed how honour and love can get you
killed in a world of treacherous politics.

00:16:38.569 --> 00:16:43.260
What’s the meaning of Arya jumping from
nowhere to kill the Night King?

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.639
That it’s cool to be a ninja?

00:16:44.639 --> 00:16:49.970
That Arya’s dehumanising murderous hate-fuelled
quest was good?

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:52.290
And where does that leave Jon and Daenerys?

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:56.970
If their destiny isn’t about beating the
white walkers, what is it about?

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:58.740
Taking the Iron Throne?

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:03.300
The whole point of the walkers is to show
that the Throne is irrelevant – human greed

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:06.750
and pride will just lead to our self-destruction.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:11.830
The walkers are an apocalyptic threat that
forces humanity to abandon their power struggles

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:17.920
and unite – the north, the wildlings, and
Daenerys came together to face a true enemy.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:24.150
But suddenly, that’s all over in Episode
3 – so will Jon and Dany now fight another

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:26.630
yet war for the Throne, against Cersei?

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.960
Why include the white walkers in the story
if they’re just a stepping stone to more

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.420
human war and petty politics?

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:38.100
Was the ancient ice demon apocalypse just
a warmup for the war against a drunk queen

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:41.020
and her pal the horny pirate?

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:45.020
Thrones author George Martin says his series
will end like the Lord of the Rings books,

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:47.520
with the Scouring of the Shire.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:51.500
In the final chapters of Rings, after the
good guys beat Sauron, the hobbits return

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.810
to the Shire and have to deal with Saruman.

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:59.120
It’s a bittersweet epilogue that shows that
the world is saved, but it’s also changed,

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.720
and its heroes have too.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.940
Maybe Thrones will do something similar.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:08.720
The big bad white walkers are defeated, but
taking Cersei off the Throne will be a time

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:14.030
to reflect on how the last eight seasons have
scarred Westeros and its people.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:18.700
But there are three long episodes left – and
if they’re filled with more big battles

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:23.130
and power struggles, that would undercut the
whole point of the walkers as a metaphor for

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.420
how terrible and pointless war is.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.970
We also learned nothing new about the white
walkers – no great revelations of their

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.330
motivations or origins.

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:38.120
Nothing about these spirals, or the babies,
or the deeper mysteries hinted in the books.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:42.830
And maybe that’s fine – the white walkers
aren’t characters, they’re a device.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:47.560
Like zombies in other stories, their purpose
is to push the human characters to extremes,

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:51.760
to show what they’re really made of, and
make them do extraordinary things.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:56.050
But in this episode, the main characters did
nothing new.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.770
Jon and Daenerys were brave.

00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:58.940
Arya was badass.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.350
Tyrion drank wine.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:02.410
Bran was confusing.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:07.730
We did get neat conclusions for Theon and
Jorah and Beric and Mel – but these are

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:09.100
secondary characters.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.760
You’d think the final confrontation with
the ultimate bad guys should’ve brought

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.500
out something climactic from the main characters.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.390
You’d also think that at least one main
character would have died.

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:23.960
But in the end, the white walkers just didn’t
impact the story that much.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.910
Walder Frey killed more important characters
than the Night King did.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:32.210
All the walkers really was bring Jon and Daenerys
together.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:36.840
And if Jon and Dany’s alliance just leads
to more war, it’s hard to see the point

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:37.840
of the walkers.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.260
And sure, maybe there’ll be a twist.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:45.320
Maybe the Night King will respawn at the spiral
tree for Round 2, and some climax with Jon

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:48.300
and Dany will happen after all.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:53.550
Maybe Bran was up to something with his magic
– we still dunno what he was doing all battle,

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.830
or what his arc is meant to mean.

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.820
We’ll just have to wait and see.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.260
Game of Thrones ends in a few weeks.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:06.330
The Game of Thrones books go deep into prophecy,
with intricate hints and symbolism.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.290
But we’re also warned against prophecy.

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:13.440
One of the coolest characters in the books
who doesn’t appear in the show is Marwyn

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:18.510
the Mage, a sort of rogue professor, a paranoid
maverick maester.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:22.820
He talks about the prophecy of Azor Ahai,
that hints that Jon or Daenerys will beat

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.660
the white walkers, and he says he doesn’t
trust it.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:31.790
He compares prophecy to a “treacherous woman”
who gives “pleasure” until “her teeth

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:37.520
snap shut” – “That is the nature of
prophecy … Prophecy will bite your prick

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:43.470
off every time” . You can hear all about
Marwyn and Azor Ahai for free today by signing

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.590
